WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.064 --> 00:00:16.046
and Mandy had never seen a square dance before.

2
00:00:17.206 --> 00:00:19.728
Four musicians stood in a corner of the room.

3
00:00:20.849 --> 00:00:27.974
Each one held a different instrument: a violin, a banjo, a bass fiddle, and a guitar.

4
00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:31.136
"Everybody, grab your partners!"

5
00:00:32.016 --> 00:00:35.637
shouted the man with the violin, and the band began to play.

6
00:00:35.657 --> 00:00:40.879
"Let's try it," said Vinnie, taking Mandy's hand.

7
00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:45.460
The dancers smiled and laughed as they whirled around the floor.

8
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.001
"This is hard!"

9
00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:52.542
gasped Mandy, trying to do the dance steps.

10
00:00:52.562 --> 00:00:55.563
"Just don't step on my feet!"

11
00:00:56.244 --> 00:00:57.004
shouted Vinnie.

12
00:00:58.168 --> 00:01:01.930
Suddenly an old man ran onto the dance floor, shouting.

13
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.172
"There's going to be a shootout!"

14
00:01:06.513 --> 00:01:09.555
The music stopped, and Nellie ran to the children.

15
00:01:09.575 --> 00:01:11.976
"What's a shootout?"

16
00:01:12.396 --> 00:01:13.117
Mandy asked.

17
00:01:13.137 --> 00:01:17.780
"It's when two men fight with guns," explained Nellie.

18
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.983
"Young Foster and Wild Bill Hickok are outside!"

19
00:01:24.043 --> 00:01:25.104
yelled the old man.

20
00:01:26.324 --> 00:01:28.946
Hearing this, people ran into the street.

21
00:01:30.187 --> 00:01:32.369
Everyone wanted to watch the shootout.

22
00:01:32.389 --> 00:01:34.530
"Who's Wild Bill?"

23
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.131
Vinnie asked Nellie.

24
00:01:36.151 --> 00:01:40.615
"He's the famous sheriff from Abilene," she replied.

25
00:01:40.635 --> 00:01:43.617
"And the best shot in the West.

26
00:01:44.918 --> 00:01:46.959
He comes to Dodge City to play cards.

27
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:48.901
He's good at that too."

28
00:01:48.921 --> 00:01:53.384
"Come on, Mandy," said Vinnie, grabbing her hand.

29
00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.829
"Vinnie, I don't like guns!"

30
00:01:57.589 --> 00:02:00.029
cried Mandy, but he pulled her along.

31
00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.650
People had gathered along the street.

32
00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.391
They watched the two men in the middle of the road.

33
00:02:08.732 --> 00:02:12.633
Standing about fifty meters apart, the men faced each other.

34
00:02:12.653 --> 00:02:17.134
"You're a cheat, Foster," said one of the men.

35
00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:20.455
He had long hair and wore two guns.

36
00:02:20.475 --> 00:02:24.596
"You can't prove it, Wild Bill," shouted the other.

37
00:02:25.632 --> 00:02:29.013
He wiggled his fingers and seemed ready to draw his guns.

38
00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:32.935
"Now gentlemen, you know the rules."

39
00:02:34.015 --> 00:02:37.397
Another man walked over and stood between the gunfighters.

40
00:02:37.417 --> 00:02:41.338
"Hey, Mandy, there's Cookie and Frank!"

41
00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:42.639
Vinnie pointed.

42
00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:46.160
The cowboys were watching the shootout too.

43
00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:50.602
"Vinnie! Doesn't this remind you of the photo?"

44
00:02:51.582 --> 00:02:52.243
asked Mandy.

45
00:02:53.323 --> 00:02:57.317
She pulled the photo out of her pocket, and it was glowing blue.

46
00:02:58.598 --> 00:03:02.740
She saw that the two men in the street were the same as in the photo.

47
00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:08.064
"Calm down, Wild Bill," said a woman in a red dress.

48
00:03:09.244 --> 00:03:12.586
She came out of the saloon holding some coins in her hand.

49
00:03:12.606 --> 00:03:21.692
"Foster is just a kid—" Suddenly, she tripped and the coins flew high into the air.

50
00:03:23.356 --> 00:03:29.479
Wild Bill drew his guns as fast as lightning and shot the five coins one after the other.

51
00:03:30.399 --> 00:03:32.120
The coins never hit the ground.

52
00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.241
The crowd cheered.

53
00:03:34.261 --> 00:03:36.842
"Vinnie! This is it!"

54
00:03:37.522 --> 00:03:40.783
Mandy said excitedly as the photo glowed red.

55
00:03:43.384 --> 00:03:47.206
The children shut their eyes and fell down the dark tunnel.

56
00:03:50.607 --> 00:03:52.228
They landed back in the attic.

57
00:03:53.372 --> 00:03:58.540
"We didn't get to see the shootout," said Vinnie, disappointed.
